# Park the cell: the arm at its folded configuration, the hand at its rest posture.
#
# Served by `home_node`, which is a RESIDENT node -- it comes up with the cell and
# stays up, and every trip home is a goal on this action rather than another run
# of the process. That is the whole reason this interface exists: homing used to
# mean launching the node, watching it move, and killing it again.
#
# THE TARGET IS NOT IN THE GOAL, deliberately. Home is a property of the cell, not
# of the caller: the arm's folded configuration is `RobotProfile.arm_home` and the
# hand's rest posture is the hand's own (see `home_node`'s docstring for why that
# is the zero command on a tendon hand and `default_pose()` on a joint one). A
# goal that could name its own target would be a one-waypoint `PlayPlan` wearing
# this action's name, and the two would drift.
#
# MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE WITH PLAYBACK. This action and `PlayPlan` publish to the same
# servo and hand command topics, and nothing but the operator sequences them. A
# goal is REJECTED while the cell-wide e-stop is engaged and while another home is
# already running, and a running goal ABORTS the moment the stop is pressed.
#
# CANCELLING is always accepted: a cancel is how an operator stops a move that is
# going somewhere they did not expect, and a stop request that can be refused is
# not a stop request. The arm halts within one tick of the control loop.

# --- Goal ---
# Both channels are skipped by NEGATION so that a default-constructed goal --
# `ros2 action send_goal ... "{}"` -- homes the whole cell, which is what someone
# who typed no fields meant. A goal with both set is rejected rather than treated
# as a no-op.
bool skip_arm                       # leave the arm where it is
bool skip_hand                      # leave the hand where it is
float64 timeout                     # seconds; 0 means the node's own `timeout`
                                    # parameter, which is the answer unless a
                                    # caller has a reason of its own
---
# --- Result ---
bool success                        # reached home inside the timeout
string message                      # markdown, for the operator's status line --
                                    # the same sentence the ~/go_home service
                                    # returns, so the two cannot describe the
                                    # same outcome differently
float64 joint_error                 # rad, worst arm joint at the end
float64 hand_error                  # worst driven actuator at the end, in
                                    # hand_units
string hand_units                   # "mm" or "rad" -- what hand_error is in,
                                    # which follows the hand's command_kind
float64 elapsed                     # wall seconds
---
# --- Feedback ---
float64 joint_error                 # rad, worst arm joint right now
float64 hand_error                  # in hand_units, as above
float64 elapsed                     # wall seconds so far
bool arm_at_home                    # inside `joint_tolerance`
bool hand_at_home                   # inside `hand_tolerance`
